Question: vTv Therapeutics terminated its phase 2 Elevage trial of azeliragon (NCT03980730). What reason did it give the registry, what did it tell investors, and do the two match?

Snapshot date: 2026-11-05
Research notes: The Lead hit its lookup cap and planned from what it had found.

Findings:
[{"lane": "trials", "round": 1, "brief": "Extract and review clinical registry details for NCT03980730 (the Phase 2 Elevage trial sponsored by vTv Therapeutics for azeliragon). Verify the official registry status, the date of primary completion or termination, the exact reason given for termination under 'why_stopped', and whether any results have been submitted or posted to ClinicalTrials.gov, along with any lateness calculation.", "findings": [{"claim": "NCT03980730 is a Phase 2 trial titled 'Study of Azeliragon in Patients With Mild Alzheimer's Disease and Impaired Glucose Tolerance', sponsored by vTv Therapeutics.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03980730"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Confirmed via snapshot and live ClinicalTrials.gov record."}, {"claim": "The official registry status of NCT03980730 is TERMINATED.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03980730"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Confirmed via snapshot and live record."}, {"claim": "The start date for NCT03980730 is 2019-06-27, the primary completion date is 2020-12-01, and the completion date is 2021-01-29, with an enrollment of 43 patients.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03980730"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Confirmed via registry records."}, {"claim": "The exact reason given under 'why_stopped' for NCT03980730 is 'for business reasons', categorized as business/strategic.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03980730"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Quote is exact from registry record."}, {"claim": "Results have been posted to ClinicalTrials.gov for NCT03980730, with a results first post date of 2022-01-21.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03980730"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Results posted status is true."}, {"claim": "The results due date for NCT03980730 was 2021-12-01, and results were posted 51 days late on 2022-01-21.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03980730"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Calculated days late is 51."}, {"claim": "Azeliragon has no approved applications on Drugs@FDA.", "evidence_ids": ["fda:none:azeliragon"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Checked via Drugs@FDA tool."}], "gaps": []}, {"lane": "disclosures", "round": 1, "brief": "Discrepancies table: 1 trial labelled discrepancy for nct_id NCT03980730 (1 checked by hand) (summary_evidence_id: snapshot:discrepancies:labels-discrepancy-nct-id-nct03980730). Please report this total as a finding. Search SEC EDGAR filings for vTv Therapeutics (CIK 0001641489) around the trial's discontinuation date. Identify any Form 8-K, 10-Q, or 10-K filings describing the stopping of the Phase 2 Elevage trial of azeliragon, extract the stated rationale provided to investors, and check if it matches the registry story.", "findings": [{"claim": "Discrepancies table: 1 trial labelled discrepancy for nct_id NCT03980730 (1 checked by hand) (summary_evidence_id: snapshot:discrepancies:labels-discrepancy-nct-id-nct03980730).", "evidence_ids": ["snapshot:discrepancies:labels-discrepancy-nct-id-nct03980730"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Direct summary statistic from the snapshot discrepancies table."}, {"claim": "For NCT03980730, the registry states the trial stopped for business reasons, while the 8-K filed on 2021-02-24 (Accession 0001564590-21-008154) explicitly names the Elevage study and provides an efficacy/futility reason: \"On December 15, 2020, vTv announced that the phase 2 Elevage Study of azeliragon did not meet its primary objective.\"", "evidence_ids": ["snapshot:discrepancies:labels-discrepancy-nct-id-nct03980730-sponsor-vtv-therapeuti", "sec:0001564590-21-008154"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Hand checked discrepancy between registry business reason and 8-K efficacy reason, naming this specific trial."}], "gaps": []}, {"lane": "publications", "round": 1, "brief": "Identify and analyze publications associated with NCT03980730 (azeliragon Elevage trial) in PubMed and Europe PMC databases. Review what findings and clinical outcomes are reported in the abstracts, when they were published, and whether the academic narrative around trial termination aligns with the registry and SEC disclosure stories.", "findings": [{"claim": "No results publication found for NCT03980730 in PubMed or Europe PMC.", "evidence_ids": ["pubmed:none:nct03980730"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Snapshot and PubMed search returned no results_candidates for NCT03980730."}, {"claim": "Five articles were identified that mention NCT03980730 or azeliragon as part of reviews or landscape analyses (mention_only), but none report trial-specific results.", "evidence_ids": ["pubmed:40207764", "pubmed:40462159", "pubmed:40686923", "pubmed:41090735", "pubmed:42009954"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "All identified articles are general reviews or mention-only references."}, {"claim": "Trial NCT03980730 was terminated for business reasons.", "evidence_ids": ["ctgov:NCT03980730"], "confidence": "high", "notes": "Registry record reports overall_status as TERMINATED due to business reasons."}], "gaps": ["No academic publications report clinical trial results for NCT03980730; results may exist in conference abstracts or corporate disclosures not indexed in PubMed or Europe PMC."]}]

