{"question": "vTv Therapeutics terminated its phase 2 Elevage trial of azeliragon (NCT03980730). What reason did it give the registry, what did it tell investors, and do the two match?", "report": {"answer": ["The registry explanation and the investor disclosures for the terminated Phase 2 Elevage trial of azeliragon do not match.", "While the registry states that vTv Therapeutics terminated the trial \"for business reasons,\" the company's Form 8-K filed with the SEC told investors that the study was discontinued because it \"did not meet its primary objective.\"", "Although clinical results were posted to the registry on 2022-01-21, no results publication was found in PubMed or Europe PMC."], "evidence": ["The registry lists NCT03980730 as a Phase 2 trial of azeliragon for mild Alzheimer's disease with an enrollment of 43 patients and an official status of terminated.", "The trial started on 2019-06-27, reached primary completion on 2020-12-01, and reached completion on 2021-01-29.", "The exact reason given under 'why_stopped' in the registry for NCT03980730 is 'for business reasons'.", "Results were posted to ClinicalTrials.gov on 2022-01-21, which was 51 days after the results due date of 2021-12-01.", "An SEC Form 8-K filed by vTv Therapeutics on 2021-02-24 stated that the Phase 2 Elevage study of azeliragon did not meet its primary objective and that the company discontinued development of the drug for Alzheimer's disease.", "In earlier SEC Form 8-K filings from November 2020, the company had announced its decision to conclude enrollment and finalize topline results for the study by December 2020.", "A search of PubMed and Europe PMC returned no results publication found for NCT03980730, though five articles merely mention the trial or drug.", "Drugs@FDA records show that azeliragon has no approved applications."], "differences": ["There is a discrepancy between the registry record, which attributes the termination to 'business reasons,' and the Form 8-K filed on 2021-02-24, which attributes the discontinuation to the Elevage study not meeting its primary objective.", "This trial is identified in the discrepancies database as a hand-checked case with a discrepancy between its registry status and investor disclosures."], "cant_tell": ["We cannot tell the real, complete underlying reason for the trial's termination beyond the brief why_stopped text in the registry and the summary statements in investor disclosures.", "The discrepancy between the registry's reasons and the investor filings is not proof of intent to mislead or any wrongdoing.", "Although the registry results were posted after the calculated results due date, this date is only an approximation of the FDAAA deadline, which only applies to applicable clinical trials, and since that status is not fully public, this is never evidence that the sponsor broke the law.", "It is possible that trial results published in conference abstracts, non-indexed journals, or company websites may have been missed by our searches."]}}

